# Strict TypeScript

- **No `any`.** Use precise types, generics, or `unknown` + narrowing.
- Define `interface` / `type` contracts for props, API responses and domain models in `types/`.
- Prefer `type`-only imports (`import type { Foo }`) to keep bundles lean.
- Components are typed function components; never rely on implicit `any` props.

## Example

```ts
// ❌ BAD
function Card(props: any) { return <div>{props.title}</div> }

// ✅ GOOD
interface CardProps {
  title: string;
  href?: string;
}
function Card({ title, href }: CardProps) { /* ... */ }
```
